        "problem": "Find the exact value of ${cos}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})-{sin}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}).$",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})-{sin}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
